00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.000
Fallon Looney: Yeah.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:51.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yeah. It's funny because I remember, like, VIP days used to take me six hours. Like, it actually took me, like, a whole three hours to, like, create the ads for them and then one hour for the first call. And now I just feel like I can get it done in, like, two, three hours.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:46.000
Fallon Looney: Oh my god.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:53.000
Fallon Looney: That's awesome.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:57.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Did you have anything similar at the agency you were at or no?

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:02.000
Fallon Looney: Um, in terms of, like, these kinds of calls?

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Like, creating it…

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:07.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Like, creating ads for them in one day or something.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:17.000
Fallon Looney: Oh, yes. Um, the… the way that it was structured, just, like, overall was a little differently. The… the team…

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:26.000
Fallon Looney: over there or at other agencies were, like, a lot bigger. I know that, like, Giselle's role was still.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:48.000
Fallon Looney: present in its own form, where, like, you know, you'd have either in ClickUp or Asana, like, all of the tasks that needed to get done. Um, and then, like, the… the other agencies that I worked at were really, like, only in the done-for-you, like, full service. So, where this is a little more done with you, it's…

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:06:00.000
Fallon Looney: kind of different, where you're not, like, live with the client. Um, and their structure was really, like, the ad strategy call and the messaging call.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:53.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:07.000
Fallon Looney: We're, like… the onboarding process was more consolidated, so it would be, like…

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:26.000
Fallon Looney: it would always be a full-service client. They come in, they fill out, like, kind of that intake form questionnaire, and it has stuff about, like, their business, the messaging, what have you, and then there would be a strategy call with the team, where we would cover, like, the ad strategy and the messaging strategy.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:39.000
Fallon Looney: And then after that point, like, we would just do the copy and creative, get approval, and then set everything up. So, like, all of the same things were happening, but, um…

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:51.000
Fallon Looney: slightly different and a little more, like, condensed, whereas here we kind of, you know, space it out, and there's also this, like, kind of done-with-you option. So, it's a little different.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:57.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Mm-hmm. That makes sense. It's just cool hearing different, like, structures and how it's done. Uh, okay.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:58.000
Fallon Looney: Yeah. Yeah, for sure.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:59.000
Carmen Cruickshank: Yes.

